# AI Prompting & Development Progress

The QuickBite prototype was built using **iterative AI-assisted development**, not a single prompt.

My approach was:

**Prompt → Build → Review → Identify Gap → Refine → Test**

AI accelerated implementation, while I retained ownership of the operating model, metrics, data strategy, governance, and final decisions.

---

## Prompt Progression

| Prompt | Focus | Why I Added It |
|---|---|---|
| **01 — Initial Dashboard** | Model, pipeline, QA, vendor and issue monitoring | Establish the basic AI Data Ops control room |
| **02 — Actionable Dashboard** | Recommendations, severity, sample size, priority | The first version showed problems but didn't answer **“What should Data Ops do next?”** |
| **03 — Data Segmentation** | Stable, Seasonal and Edge-Case data | Different data types require different sourcing, sampling and refresh strategies |
| **04 — Edge Case Radar** | Emerging operational risks | Move from only detecting failures to anticipating **what might fail next** |
| **05 — Agentic Workflow** | Detection → Triage → Data Strategy → Evaluation | Break AI assistance into clear operational responsibilities |
| **06 — Human Governance** | Approve / Modify / Reject + Decision Trace | AI should recommend, but humans control consequential actions |
| **07 — Data Ingestion** | CSV/JSON → Validate → Preview → Approve | Move from a static demo toward a functional Data Ops workflow |
| **08 — Dynamic Analytics** | MAE, P90, QA, readiness, cohort issues | Make approved data drive the dashboard instead of static values |
| **08 — Drill-Down** | Overview → Data → Metrics → Issues | Allow operators to move from **signal → evidence → action** |
| **Next Iteration** | UX simplification | Reduce duplication and simplify the final presentation |

